1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:06,056
Open Tools, Phone Verifications Queue.

2
00:00:06,056 --> 00:00:10,817
It lists every number that has verification data, with a tile for each

3
00:00:10,817 --> 00:00:13,260
status that adds up to the total.

4
00:00:13,831 --> 00:00:18,337
Each row shows the number, its status, the provider, how many attempts were

5
00:00:18,337 --> 00:00:22,231
made, and when the last one was, with the contact it belongs to.

6
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:24,479
Click the Failed tile.

7
00:00:24,479 --> 00:00:29,440
Failed means the last check failed and the site will try again by itself.

8
00:00:29,897 --> 00:00:35,002
Needs attention means the check failed Maximum verification attempts times in a row,

9
00:00:35,002 --> 00:00:36,874
so the site stopped trying.

10
00:00:36,874 --> 00:00:40,618
The latest error is shown in red, so you can tell a provider

11
00:00:40,618 --> 00:00:42,377
outage from a bad number.

12
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:46,686
Use Search by phone number to find a record, and the sort list

13
00:00:46,686 --> 00:00:49,880
to put the most recent or the oldest attempts first.

14
00:00:52,457 --> 00:00:57,242
To check one number again, open its Actions menu and click Verify again.

15
00:00:57,242 --> 00:01:00,494
A failed number has a Retry now button instead.

16
00:01:00,494 --> 00:01:03,500
The check is queued and runs shortly after.

17
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:07,917
Here the service cannot be reached, so the record shows the error.

18
00:01:08,486 --> 00:01:11,921
Tick several records, then click Retry selected.

19
00:01:11,921 --> 00:01:19,046
Retry all failed re-queues every failed and needs-attention record on every page that matches your search.

